A||||12||horseman||WHOA! Strange electical gremlins at work||||5||
Z||000000||horseman||12-24-2000||12:49 AM||||Hello All,<P>Here's the deal. I have good headlights with no tailights. I have no brakelights. However, I have front running(parking?)lights when the brakes are applied. I tried my hazard flashers(with headlights on) and my dash, ashtrays,and lighter socket flashed. Nothing from the rear lighting assembly though.<P>The wiring looks to be good and unmodified. No tape or splices. Does anyboody have any suggestions?<P>Charlie||||reg||5
Z||000001||theogre||12-24-2000||11:08 AM||||Start taking apart light assemblies and following wires. Sounds like broken grounds. Also check ground ties on the block and the thin one from the battery to the body.||||reg||1
Z||000002||hugh||12-24-2000||01:49 PM||||I agree with Theogre,when you get crazy things like that it is usually caused by a bad ground.||||reg||1
Z||000003||horseman||12-24-2000||08:22 PM||||Hi Guys and Merry Christmas,<BR>Thanks for the ideas. What other grounds besides the neg./body ground are there on the 84? Where are they located? I have noticed intermittent strange problems at times. Like sometimes the stereo won't come on for a while, then mysteriously it powers up. The first few times that I used the defrost; it blew alot of smoky vapor in the car. I even had smoke under the front hatch. Could this be from the car sitting awhile? It seems to be gone now. Good thing, as I thought the car was having an electrical fire or heater core problem at first.<P>Charlie||||reg||1
Z||000004||strdream||12-24-2000||08:53 PM||||Charlie<BR>That feed back in the brake light circuit tells me to look for a rear harness that is pinched or damaged. Use a circuit tester on your rear lights, even if there is a ground problem you will still have power if the wireing is good.<BR>Look for that source of smoke under the hood.  The defroster get it's incoming air from around there. <BR>At this time I would treat all three problems as separate.<BR>I don't know of a GM sound system that is that old and still works right and was never repaired.<BR>Ross   ||||reg||1
Z||000005||horseman||12-24-2000||11:43 PM||||Thanks and Merry X-mas Ross,<BR> I'll try your suggestions in the morning.<BR>Man I hope this works!<P>Charlie||||reg||1
Z||000006||strdream||12-25-2000||07:50 PM||||Charlie<BR>If all of the grounds to the rear are gone it can cause a feedback to the front.<BR>The next step after you find that there is power to the rear lights (assuming that you do get power to the rear) is to test for power on the ground side of the light sockets.  If you get power there than you have no ground.  (All of this is assuming that the light bulbs and sockets are good.) Try adding a temperary jumper wire from the ground side of a light to a good ground.<BR>If the lights work right, repair the grounds.<BR>I can't recall for sure the location of the grounds but I think I remember one on right side of the engine bay. it was several black wires on it.<BR>Good luck <BR>Ross ||||reg||1
Z||000007||FieroJoe||12-25-2000||07:56 PM||||Hopefully that smoke you are talking about wasnt a wire shorting to ground and burning all of its insulation off.  You would have probably recognized the smell though, burning rubber and copper.<BR>Hope you get it all worked out right, the earlier models were known for electrical idiosyncrasis.||||reg||1
Z||000008||horseman||12-25-2000||09:14 PM||||Thanks again Guys,<BR>I didn't have time to check the ground connections today. Christmas dinner and all. The smoke didn't really have an odor. It was more like a heavy vapor. It seemed to be originating from behind the the washer fluid tank. I thought that it might have been the heatercore or hoses. Now I think that it must have been the A/C compressor? Doesn't it run when the defroster is engaged? Confused,<BR>Charlie||||reg||14
Z||000009||horseman||12-26-2000||11:33 PM||||WOW, Now I am really confused. Today I started the car to show the problem to a friend of mine. Still no tails,brakelights or turn indicators. Then about a half hour later, I was showing it to another friend of mine and EVERYTHING worked fine. He thought I was nuts. After he left, same problems as before! <P>Where exactly are all of the grounds that I should be looking into? I am almost considering only driving the car with my second friend riding shotgun. He would definetly put a damper on my social life though. I love the guy like a brother but he is a nerd!<BR>Please Help Guys and Gals,<P>Charlie||||reg||5
Z||000010||horseman||12-27-2000||02:04 AM||||Bump, Help! Please. I will check with you in the morning.<BR>Thanks,<BR>Charlie||||reg||1
Z||000011||2xsess||12-27-2000||03:29 PM||||Just have that one friend of yours ride around with you all the time <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Sorry, I can't help. Just had to put in my stupid comment.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000012||strdream||12-27-2000||08:01 PM||||Carlie<BR>The more you do, the more you point to ground trouble.  My book is for '85 and shows the ground bolted to the "center of the rear bulkhead"  The picture looks like it right below the ECM between the seats on top of the center counsole.  That means the ground circuit goes to the rear thru the bulkhead connector towards the center of the car from the battery which is where I would look first for the trouble.  Ground is black.<BR>Ross<BR>||||reg||1
